.TH SONGREC 1 "November 2025" "songrec 0.4.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
songrec \- open-source Shazam client for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B songrec
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SongRec is an open-source Shazam client for Linux, written in Rust.
It allows you to recognize songs from audio files or from the microphone.
.PP
When launched without arguments, SongRec starts the graphical user interface.
When a filename is provided, it recognizes the song from that audio file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help information
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Display version information
.TP
.I FILE
Audio file to recognize (when provided, runs in CLI mode)
.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 2
Recognize audio from arbitrary audio files
.IP \(bu 2
Recognize audio from the microphone
.IP \(bu 2
GUI and command line interface for file recognition
.IP \(bu 2
History of recognized songs, exportable to CSV
.IP \(bu 2
Continuous song detection from microphone with device selection
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch GUI:
.B songrec
.TP
Recognize song from file:
.B songrec /path/to/audio/file.mp3
